{#- The failure message for `cs-agent maintenance on --wait` (tasks/hold.yml),
    one per outcome of the node_upgrade_classify_on filter. Every message says
    whether the node is held and what to do. This runs only on a FRESH run, so
    no state file exists and nothing has been stopped -- which is the one
    situation where suggesting `cs-agent maintenance off` is safe. -#}
{%- set r = node_upgrade_on_result -%}
{%- set host = inventory_hostname -%}
{%- set err = (node_upgrade_on.stderr | default('') | trim | regex_replace('\s+', ' '))[-600:] -%}
{%- set nothing = 'Nothing was stopped and no upgrade state was written.' -%}
{%- if r.outcome == 'timeout' -%}
{{ host }} IS HELD (local maintenance hold set) but did not go quiet within {{ node_upgrade_maintenance_timeout }}s
(quiesce: {{ r.quiesce | default('?') }}). Still in flight:
{# described as cs-agent's describeInFlight does: kind, volume, short id unless it IS the kind #}
{% for w in r.running %}{{ w.kind }}{{ (' ' ~ w.volume) if w.volume | default('') else '' }}{{ (' [' ~ (w.id | string)[:12] ~ ']') if w.id | default('') and w.id != w.kind else '' }}{{ '; ' if not loop.last else '' }}{% endfor %}{{ 'nothing listed (docker could not list the backup containers)' if not r.running else '' }}.
{{ nothing }} Clear the hold with `cs-agent maintenance off` on the node, then re-run once that work
has finished (or with a longer node_upgrade_maintenance_timeout). A re-run refuses while the hold
is still in place: this playbook never adopts a hold it did not record placing.
{%- elif r.outcome == 'not_placed' -%}
{{ host }} is NOT held: cs-agent placed no hold, because the controller has not polled it with
maintenance support in the last 120s (a controller older than 9.8.0, or one that is not reaching
this node's agent), and still had not after {{ node_upgrade_hold_not_placed_retries }} more attempts
{{ node_upgrade_hold_not_placed_delay }}s apart. {{ nothing }} Check the controller's version and its connection to the node,
then re-run.
{%- elif r.outcome == 'unconfirmed' -%}
{{ host }} IS HELD locally and quiet, but the controller did not confirm the hold within
{{ node_upgrade_maintenance_timeout }}s. Without that confirmation the controller may still act on
the node (health checks, recovery, placement). {{ nothing }} Clear the hold with
`cs-agent maintenance off` on the node, check the controller is >= 9.8.0 and polling the node, then
re-run.
{%- elif r.outcome == 'cleared' -%}
{{ host }} is NOT held: the local hold was cleared while cs-agent was waiting (somebody ran
`cs-agent maintenance off`). {{ nothing }} Find out who is working on the node before re-running.
{%- elif r.outcome == 'interrupted' -%}
{{ host }} IS HELD: `cs-agent maintenance on` was interrupted (SIGINT/SIGTERM) and left its hold in
place. {{ nothing }} Clear the hold with `cs-agent maintenance off` on the node, then re-run.
{%- elif r.outcome == 'error' -%}
cs-agent on {{ host }} failed: {{ r.error }} (exit {{ r.rc }}). It could not read its own state, so
whether a hold was placed is UNKNOWN. {{ nothing }} Run `cs-agent maintenance status` on the node; if
it shows a local hold with reason `{{ node_upgrade_reason }}`, clear it with
`cs-agent maintenance off`. Fix the agent, then re-run.
{%- elif r.outcome == 'no_output' -%}
`cs-agent maintenance on` on {{ host }} exited {{ r.rc }} without a JSON result{{ (': ' ~ err) if err else '' }}.
Whether a hold was placed is UNKNOWN. {{ nothing }} Run `cs-agent maintenance status` on the node;
if it shows a local hold with reason `{{ node_upgrade_reason }}`, clear it with
`cs-agent maintenance off`. Then re-run.
{%- else -%}
`cs-agent maintenance on` on {{ host }} exited {{ r.rc }}{{ (': ' ~ err) if err else '' }}.
The node {{ 'IS HELD (local hold set)' if r.held else 'is NOT held' }}. {{ nothing }}
{{ 'Clear the hold with `cs-agent maintenance off` on the node, then re-run.' if r.held else 'Re-run once the cause is fixed.' }}
{%- endif -%}
